  <result aggregation-status="0" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tier 2 Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improved Governance</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">In partnership with Australian Government Agencies, the Mekong-Australia Partnership on Transnational Crime (MAP-TNC) supported 74 Mekong government institutions to improve their governance and capacity to counter financial crime, child sexual exploitation and illicit drugs in the Mekong subregion. The support was delivered through 22 activities and to 503 officers. With the support provided, the recipients increased their technical capacity and changed their workplace practices. For example, following the Regional Cryptocurrency and Blockchain investigations course, Mekong law enforcement officers are now able to trace illicit cryptocurrency flows and identify the source of illicit digital assets, which are broadly used in Special Economic Zones and known to be a common money laundering method. This has led to a change in investigation practices for tracing illicit digital assets by Mekong law enforcement agencies. MAP-TNC also supported a joint research project between Thailand&#x2019;s Department of Special Investigation and Chulalongkorn University on &#x201c;Research and Development on Misuse of Technology (Forced Criminality)&#x201d;, exploring how victims are trafficked into scam centres in Mekong. This research has been endorsed by Thailand&#x2019;s Minister of Justice.</narrative>
    </description>
